# Core-side requests. Lovable application traffic must instead invoke Supabase Edge Functions.
# These examples describe source contract 1.4.0; an older live deployment may expose older metadata.
# Set accessToken only in your HTTP client's private local environment; never commit a real JWT.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:6086
@accessToken =
@organization = 11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111
@scan = 22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222
# Replace with the sessionId returned by the reader session admission.
@readerSession = 44444444-4444-4444-8444-444444444444
# Copy snapshot.documentId from the observation response, without interpreting it as instructions.
@documentId = replace-with-observed-document-id
# Generate once for a new admission; reuse after an unconfirmed response.
@requestId = 33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333
# Copy both values from a separately retained operator import receipt in this workspace.
# An import is not a scan admission or permission grant.
@archive = 55555555-5555-4555-8555-555555555555
@indexSha256 = replace-with-retained-index-sha256

### Bounded original-file metadata; follow nextOffset with the same retained identity
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workspaces/{{organization}}/archives/{{archive}}/manifest
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"indexSha256":"{{indexSha256}}","offset":0}

### Exact original bytes; follow nextOffset, decode base64 and verify whole fileSha256
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workspaces/{{organization}}/archives/{{archive}}/file
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"indexSha256":"{{indexSha256}}","path":"evidence-manifest.json","offset":0}

### Published protocol; anonymous, no secrets
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json

### Actual listener readiness; not proof of user sign-in or public MCP
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/ready

### Current server-verified user
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/session
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Idempotently create or resume this subject's workspace
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workspace
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Read a currently visible workspace
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workspaces/{{organization}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### At most fifty recent runs; check hasMore
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workspaces/{{organization}}/scans
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Admit only the server-selected, input-free fixture
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workspaces/{{organization}}/scans
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"requestId":"{{requestId}}"}

### Report: execution and evidence availability are separate facts
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workspaces/{{organization}}/scans/{{scan}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Expected 401; no user credential supplied
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/session

### Open an ephemeral subject-owned read-only Foundation fixture; body must stay empty
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workspaces/{{organization}}/reader-sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Read owned session metadata; same subject and current workspace membership required
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workspaces/{{organization}}/reader-sessions/{{readerSession}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Fresh semantics, without input, recordings or a verified goal claim
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workspaces/{{organization}}/reader-sessions/{{readerSession}}/observations
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Pure browse navigation; repeat commands to advance the virtual cursor without moving focus
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workspaces/{{organization}}/reader-sessions/{{readerSession}}/commands
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"command":"NextHeading","expectedDocumentId":"{{documentId}}"}

### Page transient command events; continue with nextAfterSequence while hasMore is true
# timelineTruncated means later history was not retained, even when hasMore becomes false.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workspaces/{{organization}}/reader-sessions/{{readerSession}}/timeline
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"afterSequence":0,"limit":100}

### Page actual state nodes, ReaderCursor edges and fresh snapshot evidence together
# Retention is transient. traceTruncated means later commands were omitted; hasMore only covers retained pages.
# RefreshedFromStateId is an observation link; zero input and false goal verification remain explicit.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workspaces/{{organization}}/reader-sessions/{{readerSession}}/trace
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"afterSequence":0,"limit":20}

### Acknowledge actual native cleanup; 503 means cleanup is unconfirmed
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/workspaces/{{organization}}/reader-sessions/{{readerSession}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
